// CHANGELOG 1.1.1:
// - Bonus overlay repositioned to anchor on the image wrapper (bottom, same positioning
//   context as the quality badge) instead of the title element, and given a background
//   pill matching the quality badge's themed background. Fixes bonus text overlapping
//   into the tile below it and being unreadable against item images.
//
// CHANGELOG 1.1.0 (audit fixes):
// - Bonus overlay is now absolutely positioned instead of being inserted into normal
//   block flow. A previous version reportedly caused Item Market's infinite scroll to
//   keep auto-loading pages, because injecting normal-flow content into every tile grew
//   total list height right after each batch loaded, tricking the page's own
//   "near bottom" scroll check into firing again. Quality badge was already an overlay
//   and was never the cause.
// - matchToCache() no longer blindly takes the first price+stat match. If more than one
//   cached item shares the same price/stats, the tile is skipped instead of risking a
//   wrong match (previously a silent mismatch was possible).
// - itemMarket cache is now capped (MAX_CACHE_ITEMS) and is cleared on same-page
//   navigation (e.g. changing category/search within Item Market), reducing both memory
//   growth and match-collision risk over a long session.
// - Processed-element tracking now uses a content-derived key (WeakMap) instead of a
//   plain WeakSet, so if the host page recycles a tile's DOM node for a different item
//   (virtualized lists), the stale badge/bonus overlay is detected and replaced instead
//   of silently left in place.
// - Added SPA navigation handling (pushState/replaceState/hashchange/popstate) so the
//   correct handler stays active, and reinitializes safely if the market pages are
//   client-side routed rather than fully reloaded.
// - Quality values far outside the plausible range are no longer displayed (they're a
//   strong signal of a bad cache match rather than a real reading).
// - Fetch parsing failures and unrecognized stat types now surface via console instead
//   of failing completely silently (stat-type warnings gated behind CONFIG.debug).

(function () {
    'use strict';

